---
import GuidePage from '../components/GuidePage.astro';
import NumberField from '../components/NumberField.astro';
import SexField from '../components/SexField.astro';

const creatinineUnits = [
	{ value: 'mg/dL', label: 'mg/dL' },
	{ value: 'umol/L', label: 'µmol/L' },
];
---

<GuidePage
	title="Creatinine Clearance Calculator (Cockcroft-Gault Formula)"
	description="Estimate creatinine clearance in mL/min with the Cockcroft-Gault formula. Compare actual, ideal, and adjusted body weight, and see every step of the math."
	h1="Creatinine clearance calculator (Cockcroft-Gault)"
	path="/creatinine-clearance-calculator"
	crumb="Creatinine Clearance Calculator"
	kind="tool"
	modified="2026-11-03"
	related={['/egfr-vs-creatinine-clearance', '/', '/ckd-epi-calculator', '/creatinine-converter']}
>
	<Fragment slot="intro">
		<p>
			Creatinine clearance (CrCl) estimates how much blood your kidneys clear of creatinine each
			minute. The Cockcroft-Gault formula calculates it from age, sex, weight, and serum
			creatinine, and it is still the estimate many drug-dosing references use. Add your height to
			compare results across all three common weight choices.
		</p>
	</Fragment>

	<div slot="tool" class="rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated p-4 sm:p-6">
		<form id="crcl-form" class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2" novalidate>
			<NumberField id="creatinine" label="Serum creatinine" placeholder="1.00" unitOptions={creatinineUnits} unitName="creatinine-unit" wide />
			<NumberField id="age" label="Age" placeholder="60" step="1" unit="years" />
			<SexField />
			<NumberField id="weight" label="Actual body weight" placeholder="70" unit="kg" />
			<NumberField id="height" label="Height (optional)" placeholder="170" unit="cm" required={false} hint="Needed for ideal and adjusted weight. Devine ideal weight applies from 152.4 cm (5 ft)." />
			<div class="sm:col-span-2">
				<button type="submit" class="w-full rounded-pill bg-link px-6 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-white transition-colors hover:bg-link-deep focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-link sm:w-auto">
					Calculate creatinine clearance
				</button>
			</div>
		</form>
		<div id="result-region" aria-live="polite"></div>
	</div>

	<h2>The Cockcroft-Gault formula</h2>
	<pre>CrCl (mL/min) = [(140 − Age) × Weight (kg)] / (72 × Scr (mg/dL))
Multiply by 0.85 if female

With creatinine in µmol/L:
CrCl (mL/min) = [(140 − Age) × Weight (kg) × 1.23] / Scr (µmol/L)    male
CrCl (mL/min) = [(140 − Age) × Weight (kg) × 1.04] / Scr (µmol/L)    female</pre>

	<h3>Worked example</h3>
	<p>
		A 60-year-old man weighing 80 kg with a serum creatinine of 1.2 mg/dL:
		(140 − 60) × 80 = 6,400, and 72 × 1.2 = 86.4. Dividing gives a creatinine clearance of
		<strong>74 mL/min</strong>. A woman with the same numbers would be 74.1 × 0.85 =
		<strong>63 mL/min</strong>.
	</p>

	<h2>Which body weight should you use?</h2>
	<p>
		The original 1976 study used actual body weight, but it can overestimate clearance in people
		with obesity. Drug references and hospitals differ on which weight to use, so check the drug
		label or your local policy. This calculator shows all three rather than choosing for you.
	</p>
	<div class="table-wrap">
		<table>
			<caption class="sr-only">Body weight options for Cockcroft-Gault</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Weight</th><th scope="col">How it is calculated</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><th scope="row">Actual</th><td>Measured body weight</td></tr>
				<tr><th scope="row">Ideal (Devine)</th><td>Male: 50 kg + 2.3 kg per inch over 5 ft. Female: 45.5 kg + 2.3 kg per inch over 5 ft.</td></tr>
				<tr><th scope="row">Adjusted</th><td>Ideal + 0.4 × (actual − ideal)</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>

	<h2>What is a normal creatinine clearance?</h2>
	<p>
		MedlinePlus lists a normal range of 97 to 137 mL/min for men and 88 to 128 mL/min for women.
		Normal values fall with age and vary slightly between labs, so your own result needs to be read
		by a clinician who knows your history.
	</p>

	<h2>Creatinine clearance vs eGFR</h2>
	<p>
		The two numbers answer different questions and use different units. CrCl is in mL/min and
		reflects your actual body size. eGFR is in mL/min/1.73m² and is scaled to a standard body size,
		which makes it the one used for <a href="/ckd-stages">CKD staging</a>. To get an eGFR, use the
		<a href="/ckd-epi-calculator">CKD-EPI calculator</a>, and see
		<a href="/egfr-vs-creatinine-clearance">eGFR vs creatinine clearance</a> for the full comparison.
	</p>

	<h2>When this estimate is less reliable</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Kidney function that is changing quickly, such as acute kidney injury, because the formula assumes stable creatinine.</li>
		<li>Very high or very low muscle mass, since creatinine comes from muscle.</li>
		<li>Pregnancy, and people under 18. For children, use the <a href="/pediatric-gfr-calculator">pediatric GFR calculator</a>.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Do not change a medicine dose based on this page. Ask your prescriber or pharmacist.</p>

	<h2>Sources</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Cockcroft DW, Gault MH. Prediction of creatinine clearance from serum creatinine. <em>Nephron</em>. 1976;16:31&ndash;41.</li>
		<li><a href="https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/003611.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MedlinePlus: Creatinine clearance tests</a>.</li>
		<li>Devine BJ. Gentamicin therapy. <em>Drug Intell Clin Pharm</em>. 1974;8:650&ndash;655.</li>
	</ul>
</GuidePage>

<script>
	import {
		adjustedBodyWeightKg,
		calculateCockcroftGault,
		idealBodyWeightKg,
		type CreatinineUnit,
		type Sex,
	} from '../lib/gfr';
	import { readChoice, readNumber, resultHtml } from '../lib/result-html';

	const form = document.getElementById('crcl-form');
	const region = document.getElementById('result-region');

	form?.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
		e.preventDefault();
		if (!region) return;
		const creatinine = readNumber('creatinine', 0.01, 3000, 'Enter a creatinine value greater than 0.');
		const age = readNumber('age', 18, 120, 'This formula is for adults. Enter an age between 18 and 120.');
		const weightKg = readNumber('weight', 1, 500, 'Enter a body weight greater than 0.');
		if (creatinine === null || age === null || weightKg === null) {
			region.innerHTML = '';
			return;
		}
		const creatinineUnit = readChoice<CreatinineUnit>('creatinine-unit');
		const sex = readChoice<Sex>('sex');
		const crcl = (kg: number) => calculateCockcroftGault({ creatinine, creatinineUnit, age, sex, weightKg: kg }).egfr;

		const heightCm = Number((document.getElementById('height') as HTMLInputElement).value);
		const ideal = heightCm > 0 ? idealBodyWeightKg(heightCm, sex) : null;
		let comparison = '';
		if (ideal !== null) {
			const adjusted = adjustedBodyWeightKg(weightKg, ideal);
			const rows: [string, number][] = [['Actual', weightKg], ['Ideal', ideal], ['Adjusted', adjusted]];
			comparison = `<table class="mt-4 w-full text-left text-sm">
				<caption class="sr-only">Creatinine clearance by body weight</caption>
				<thead><tr class="border-b border-hairline"><th scope="col" class="py-2 font-medium text-ink">Weight used</th><th scope="col" class="py-2 font-medium text-ink">kg</th><th scope="col" class="py-2 font-medium text-ink">CrCl (mL/min)</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>${rows
					.map(([name, kg]) => `<tr class="border-b border-hairline-soft"><th scope="row" class="py-2 font-normal text-body">${name}</th><td class="py-2 text-body">${kg.toFixed(1)}</td><td class="py-2 font-medium text-ink">${crcl(kg)}</td></tr>`)
					.join('')}</tbody>
			</table>`;
		}
		region.innerHTML = resultHtml(calculateCockcroftGault({ creatinine, creatinineUnit, age, sex, weightKg }), comparison);
		region.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'nearest' });
	});
</script>
